IMPORT prelude

-- Loans (International Banks) Act 1958 (Singapore) -- who "the Bank" and a "statutory authority" are (s 2), how the loan money may
-- be spent (ss 3(2), 6), when a statutory authority may borrow from the Bank and charge its property (s 5), the Government's
-- guarantee and what follows from it (ss 7-10), arbitration (s 11), and the effect of the agreements in Singapore law: tax remission,
-- exchange control and the negative pledge (s 12).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/LIBA1958.txt. The deposit says the revised edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; the only amendment
-- annotated in the body is [11/91] on s 7(1), and the legislative history ends with Act 11 of 1991 (commencement 30 November 1991).
-- The arrangement of sections at the top of the deposit is out of step by one (it lists a blank "1." and numbers "Short title" 2);
-- the BODY's numbering (s 1 short title to s 12) is followed here.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0182 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked
-- a sharper question yet. The honest answer is: very little directly. The Act governs the Government and statutory authorities as
-- borrowers from the IBRD and the Asian Development Bank. A private person or business meets it mainly as a creditor or bondholder
-- of a statutory authority (s 5(4) charges, s 12(3) negative pledge), as a party affected by a tax remission order (s 12(2)(a)), or
-- as someone whose payment is outside the Exchange Control Act (s 12(2)(b)).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 3(3)-(5) and s 4 (who signs for the Government, presenting agreements to Parliament, other borrowing powers),
-- s 5(3) and (5) (powers additional; issuing bonds), s 7(2) (form and signature of a guarantee), s 9(3), s 12(1) beyond its
-- effect through s 12(2). The Constitution (Article 144) and the Development Fund Act 1959 are referred to but not read.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Loans (International Banks) Act 1958`

§§ `2 -- the Bank and statutory authorities`

-- s 2: "'Bank' means the International Bank for Reconstruction and Development or the Asian Development Bank".
-- "'statutory authority' means a local authority and any body incorporated directly by any written law and exercising powers vested
-- in such body by law for a public purpose."
DECLARE Lender IS ONE OF
    `the International Bank for Reconstruction and Development`
    `the Asian Development Bank`
    `the Asian Infrastructure Investment Bank`
    `the International Development Association`
    `a commercial bank`

GIVEN `the lender` IS A Lender
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the lender is the Bank` IF
    CONSIDER `the lender`
    WHEN `the International Bank for Reconstruction and Development` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Asian Development Bank` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- The two limbs are read as alternatives ("a local authority AND any body ..." lists two kinds of body). Whether a company formed
-- under the Companies Act 1967 is "incorporated directly by any written law" is an inference (here: no -- it is incorporated under a
-- general Act, not directly by one); the text does not say.
GIVEN `is a local authority` IS A BOOLEAN, `incorporated directly by a written law` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `exercises powers vested by law for a public purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a statutory authority` IF
        `is a local authority`
    OR  (`incorporated directly by a written law` AND `exercises powers vested by law for a public purpose`)

§§ `3(2) and 6 -- what the loan money may be spent on`

-- s 3(2) (Government) and s 6 (statutory authority): sums borrowed "shall be applied ... to the purposes for which they were borrowed
-- as specified in any agreement concluded with the Bank ... Provided that where any part of such a sum cannot be applied to those
-- purposes that part may be applied to such other purposes as may be approved by the Minister and the Bank."
-- Both approvals are needed, and only for a part that CANNOT be applied to the agreed purposes.
GIVEN `a purpose in the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN, `that part cannot be applied to the agreed purposes` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Minister approves` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Bank approves` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the loan money may be applied to it` IF
        `a purpose in the agreement`
    OR  (`that part cannot be applied to the agreed purposes` AND `the Minister approves` AND `the Bank approves`)

§§ `5 -- a statutory authority borrowing from the Bank`

-- s 5(1): "a statutory authority may ... with the approval in writing first obtained of the Minister borrow from the Bank".
GIVEN `the borrower is a statutory authority` IS A BOOLEAN, `the lender` IS A Lender,
      `the Minister's written approval was first obtained` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may borrow under section 5` IF
    `the borrower is a statutory authority` AND `the lender is the Bank` `the lender` AND `the Minister's written approval was first obtained`

-- s 5(2): notwithstanding its establishing law, an agreement with the Bank "shall be valid and binding on the authority if signed on
-- behalf of the authority by a person authorised thereto in writing under the seal of the statutory authority". This is a
-- SUFFICIENT condition; the rule says only whether s 5(2) itself makes the agreement binding.
GIVEN `signed by a person authorised in writing under seal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 5(2) makes the agreement binding` IF `signed by a person authorised in writing under seal`

-- s 5(4): notwithstanding its establishing law, the authority "may charge or mortgage all or any of its property (movable or
-- immovable), undertaking or revenue to secure any sum owing to the Bank in respect of sums borrowed by it under" s 5(1).
GIVEN `the debt is owed to the Bank` IS A BOOLEAN, `the debt arises from a section 5 borrowing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 5(4) allows the charge` IF `the debt is owed to the Bank` AND `the debt arises from a section 5 borrowing`

§§ `7 and 8 -- the Government guarantee, and the freeze on other borrowing`

-- s 7(1): "The Government with the President's concurrence under Article 144(1)(b) of the Constitution may ... (a) guarantee the
-- discharge by a statutory authority of its obligations under any agreement ... in respect of any borrowing authorised by section
-- 5(1) or under any bond, promissory note or other instrument issued pursuant to any such agreement". [11/91]
GIVEN `the President concurs` IS A BOOLEAN, `the borrowing is authorised by section 5(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Government may guarantee it` IF `the President concurs` AND `the borrowing is authorised by section 5(1)`

-- s 8: "So long as the Government continues to be liable under any guarantee ... the statutory authority shall not except with the
-- consent of the Minister exercise any other power to borrow possessed by it."
-- Whether a further loan from the Bank under s 5 is an "other power to borrow" is not settled by the text; s 5 already requires the
-- Minister's prior written approval, so the point matters little. Encoded for borrowing under any OTHER power.
GIVEN `a Government guarantee is outstanding` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Minister consents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may use another borrowing power` IF (NOT `a Government guarantee is outstanding`) OR `the Minister consents`

§§ `9 -- directions where default is in prospect`

-- s 9(1): where "it is made to appear to the President that there is reasonable cause to believe -- (a) that a statutory authority
-- is likely to fail or be unable to discharge any of its obligations under any agreement ... with the Bank ...; and (b) that the
-- Government is or may become liable under any guarantee ..., the President may by order give or authorise any other person to give
-- such directions". (2): the authority "shall notwithstanding any provision in the written law by which it is established comply".
GIVEN `reasonable cause to believe the authority is likely to fail` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Government is or may become liable under a guarantee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the President may order directions` IF
    `reasonable cause to believe the authority is likely to fail` AND `the Government is or may become liable under a guarantee`

§§ `10 -- repaying the Consolidated Fund`

-- s 10(1): if any sum is paid out of the Consolidated Fund under a s 7(1) guarantee, "the statutory authority shall repay that sum
-- (together with interest on it at the same rate as that payable on the loan under the agreement by the statutory authority with the
-- Bank) ... in such manner and at such time or by such instalments as the Minister may direct." The rate is the loan rate; how the
-- interest runs (period, simple or compound) is left to the Minister's direction and is not encoded.
GIVEN `the sum paid out of the Consolidated Fund` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the authority must repay` IF `the sum paid out of the Consolidated Fund` GREATER THAN 0

GIVEN `the rate on the Bank loan` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the interest rate on the repayment` IS `the rate on the Bank loan`

-- s 10(2): the Minister presents a statement to Parliament "as soon as possible after the end of each financial year beginning with
-- that in which the sum was paid and ending with that in which all liability in respect of it and any interest payable on it is
-- finally discharged". Both end years count.
GIVEN `the financial year paid` IS A NUMBER, `the financial year finally discharged` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the number of annual statements to Parliament` IS
    `the financial year finally discharged` MINUS `the financial year paid` PLUS 1

§§ `11 -- arbitration`

-- s 11: a dispute "between the Bank on the one part and the Government or a statutory authority or both on the other part" arising
-- under an agreement, guarantee or undertaking under this Act, or under an instrument issued pursuant to an agreement, "shall be
-- determined by arbitration in the manner agreed between the parties"; the award is enforceable as if made under the Arbitration Act
-- 2001, which "shall be binding on the Government". A dispute between a bondholder and the authority is not within s 11.
GIVEN `the Bank is one party` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Government or a statutory authority is the other` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `it arises under an agreement, guarantee or instrument under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 11 sends it to arbitration` IF
    `the Bank is one party` AND `the Government or a statutory authority is the other`
    AND `it arises under an agreement, guarantee or instrument under the Act`

§§ `12(2) -- tax remission and exchange control`

-- s 12(2)(a): "the Minister may provide by order published in the Gazette that any tax or duty payable under the Income Tax Act 1947
-- or the Stamp Duties Act 1929 respectively shall be remitted where such remission is necessary to give full and complete effect to
-- any such agreement". No remission without a Gazette order; no other tax is mentioned.
DECLARE Tax IS ONE OF
    `income tax`
    `stamp duty`
    `goods and services tax`
    `property tax`

GIVEN `the tax` IS A Tax
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the tax is one section 12(2)(a) reaches` IF
    CONSIDER `the tax`
    WHEN `income tax` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `stamp duty` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the tax` IS A Tax, `a Gazette order remits it` IS A BOOLEAN, `remission is necessary to give effect to the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the tax is remitted` IF
    `the tax is one section 12(2)(a) reaches` `the tax` AND `a Gazette order remits it` AND `remission is necessary to give effect to the agreement`

-- s 12(2)(b): "nothing in the provisions of the Exchange Control Act 1953 shall apply to any transaction required to effect payment in
-- any currency of any sum in accordance with the terms of any such agreement, instrument, bond or guarantee".
GIVEN `the transaction is required to pay a sum under the agreement, bond or guarantee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Exchange Control Act is disapplied` IF `the transaction is required to pay a sum under the agreement, bond or guarantee`

§§ `12(3) and (4) -- the negative pledge`

-- s 12(4): "'external debt' means any debt payable in any medium other than currency which at the time in question is legal tender
-- for the payment of private and public debt in Singapore whether the debt is payable absolutely or at the option of the creditor in
-- the other medium"; "'lien' includes mortgages, pledges, charges, privileges and priorities of any kind."
GIVEN `payable in a medium other than Singapore legal tender` IS A BOOLEAN, `the creditor may opt for another medium` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the debt is external` IF `payable in a medium other than Singapore legal tender` OR `the creditor may opt for another medium`

-- s 12(3): "Neither the Government nor any agency thereof nor any statutory authority nor any central bank for Singapore ... shall,
-- except as is otherwise agreed between the Minister and the Bank, create any lien on any of its assets as security for any external
-- debt unless it is expressly provided that the lien will ipso facto equally and rateably secure the payment of the principal and
-- interest and other charges on any loan made by ... the Bank to the Government or to a statutory authority."
-- The text does not limit the bar to a statutory authority that has itself borrowed from the Bank.
DECLARE Body IS ONE OF
    `the Government`
    `a Government agency`
    `a statutory authority`
    `the central bank`
    `a private company`

GIVEN `the body` IS A Body
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the body is bound by the negative pledge` IF
    CONSIDER `the body`
    WHEN `a private company` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the body` IS A Body, `the secured debt is external` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the lien expressly secures the Bank loans equally and rateably` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Minister and the Bank agreed otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 12(3) forbids the lien` IF
    `the body is bound by the negative pledge` `the body` AND `the secured debt is external`
    AND (NOT `the lien expressly secures the Bank loans equally and rateably`) AND (NOT `the Minister and the Bank agreed otherwise`)
